Description: map a userspace program to the kernel code it exercises
 vock runs a command and reports exactly which kernel source lines that
 command caused to execute, as an annotated HTML or terminal report.
 .
 Coverage is collected either from KCOV (per-thread, via an LD_PRELOAD shim
 that follows fork, vfork and pthread_create) or from a hardware trace unit
 with no kernel instrumentation required: Intel Processor Trace and AMD LBR
 on x86-64, CoreSight ETM on arm64.
 .
 Syscalls made by the target can be traced through any of three backends
 (ptrace, SYSCALL_USER_DISPATCH, or eBPF) and emitted either in strace format
 or as a syzkaller program. vock can also replay a syzkaller program,
 including an unmodified syzbot reproducer, and collect per-call coverage
 for it.
 .
 Reports resolve addresses through DWARF, BTF or kallsyms, and handle KASLR.
